identity:
  id: eravos.contrast-space ; label: Contrast Space ; domain: music ; family: space_and_transformation
  lineage: multiband imaging, sidechain ducking, detuned layers (beating), tension and release in bass music
  family_from: UK dubstep and grime low-end practice (technique only), psychoacoustics (beating, masking), coupled oscillators
assembles (components, tools/music/components/<id>/ — never re-implemented here):
  multiband-splitter · stereo-tools · waveshaper · unison-stack · ducker · masking-analyzer · panner · early-reflections · lfo · tension-meter · oscillator-population · relationship-graph · scale-key
adds (behaviour only this tool has):
  - each band its own place in space, its own ripple and its own duck, seen on one field
  - tension and agreement (sync) sent out as signals any tool can follow
modes: split · ripple · collide
signal_dag:
  in → multiband-splitter
  multiband-splitter → stereo-tools
  multiband-splitter → waveshaper → unison-stack → ducker
  multiband-splitter → panner → early-reflections
  masking-analyzer → ducker
  lfo → unison-stack
  ducker → stereo-tools
  early-reflections → stereo-tools
  stereo-tools → out
  tension-meter → out
  oscillator-population → relationship-graph → out
ports: in (audio), key (audio, side input for the collision), out (audio); mod out: tension, sync; mod in: release, every knob
params: Note, Beat (Hz), Voices · Pitch (display) · Split, Duck · Distance, Width, Bass mono · Rate, Swing, Lean · Hold, Release · Coupling, Spread, Count
packs (≥ 6 presets each, novelty-tested):
  - Floor Pressure — slow ripples under a mono sub, the mid ducked hard
  - Wide Threat — a dry centre, far wide throws
  - Pendulum Low — the swing lingering low, oscillatory and clean (T-91)
acceptance:
  - the tool contract (TH.toolContract): spawns clean · every preset loads in range · save → load exact · closing leaves nothing · Stop all obeyed
  - open-as-components: the wired components render the same as the tool (≤ −60 dB difference)
  - Beat 0 Hz and Duck 0 dB and Width 1: the tool passes the sound unchanged (≤ −60 dB)

